<h1>Machining</h1>

<p>Our Wrexham site houses the group's main machining base: over forty CNC turning and milling centres, including three, four and five-axis machines, working from both our own castings and customer-supplied bar and forged stock.</p>

<p>Typical tolerances held in production are &plusmn;0.02 mm on critical bores and faces, with full first-article inspection reports and coordinate measuring data supplied against the customer drawing. Fixtures and work-holding are designed in-house so that repeat orders can be set up quickly without re-proving the process each time.</p>

<p>Machined parts are frequently routed on to <a href="/products/finishing">finishing</a> for coating or plating before dispatch. Fixture and tool design work is carried out by the same team responsible for <a href="/products/tooling">tooling</a>.</p>
